    </w:p>
    <w:p>
      <w:r><w:t>Date: April 15, 2026</w:t></w:r>
    </w:p>
    <w:p/>
    <w:p>
      <w:r><w:t>Loan Request</w:t></w:r>
    </w:p>
    <w:p>
      <w:r><w:t>- Amount: ₦1,300,000</w:t></w:r>
    </w:p>
    <w:p>
      <w:r><w:t>- Purpose: Fund inventory, supplier prepayments, working capital, workspace setup and marketing to launch an owner-operated fashion/manufacturing business. Equipment purchases will be phased and funded from future profits.</w:t></w:r>
    </w:p>
    <w:p/>
    <w:p>
      <w:r><w:t>Use of Funds (₦1,300,000)</w:t></w:r>
    </w:p>
    <w:p>
      <w:r><w:t>- Inventory &amp; raw materials: ₦600,000</w:t></w:r>
    </w:p>
    <w:p>
      <w:r><w:t>- Working capital (utilities, shipping, consumables): ₦250,000</w:t></w:r>
    </w:p>
    <w:p>
      <w:r><w:t>- Supplier prepayments / bulk discounts: ₦100,000</w:t></w:r>
    </w:p>
    <w:p>
      <w:r><w:t>- Workspace setup / minor renovations: ₦100,000</w:t></w:r>
    </w:p>
    <w:p>
      <w:r><w:t>- Marketing &amp; e-commerce setup: ₦50,000</w:t></w:r>
    </w:p>
    <w:p>
      <w:r><w:t>- Contingency: ₦200,000</w:t></w:r>
    </w:p>
    <w:p/>
    <w:p>
      <w:r><w:t>Repayment Terms</w:t></w:r>
    </w:p>
    <w:p>
      <w:r><w:t>- Term: 14 months.</w:t></w:r>
    </w:p>
    <w:p>
      <w:r><w:t>- Monthly payment: ₦1,300,000 ÷ 14 ≈ ₦92,857.</w:t></w:r>
    </w:p>
    <w:p>
      <w:r><w:t>- Source: Monthly cash flow from sales; borrower prioritizes repayments from receipts.</w:t></w:r>
    </w:p>
    <w:p/>
    <w:p>
      <w:r><w:t>Collateral &amp; Controls</w:t></w:r>
    </w:p>
    <w:p>
      <w:r><w:t>- Optional: personal guarantee or other security as mutually agreed.</w:t></w:r>
    </w:p>
    <w:p/>
    <w:p>
      <w:r><w:t>Milestones</w:t></w:r>
    </w:p>
    <w:p>
      <w:r><w:t>- Month 0: Loan disbursed; inventory procured; setup and marketing initiated.</w:t></w:r>
    </w:p>
    <w:p>
      <w:r><w:t>- Months 1–2: Production and initial sales commence.</w:t></w:r>
    </w:p>
    <w:p>
      <w:r><w:t>- Months 3–14: Sales scale and monthly repayments made; complete repayment by month 14.</w:t></w:r>
    </w:p>
    <w:p/>
    <w:p>
      <w:r><w:t>Closing Statement</w:t></w:r>
    </w:p>
    <w:p>
      <w:r><w:t>I request ₦1,300,000 to start operations and build sales capacity. I will reinvest profits to acquire remaining equipment. I commit to timely monthly principal repayments of approximately ₦92,857 until the loan is repaid.</w:t></w:r>
    </w:p>
    <w:p/>
    <w:p>
      <w:r><w:t>Borrower signature: ______________________    Date: __________</w:t></w:r>
    </w:p>
    <w:p>
      <w:r><w:t>Name (printed): Abdulwasi-iu Abubakar Jafar</w:t></w:r>
    </w:p>
    <w:p>
      <w:r><w:t>Business: Fashion Marketplace</w:t></w:r>
    </w:p>
    <w:p/>
